        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): retry once on token-invalid errors 99991663/99991664 with cache invalidation (fixes #97287)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #97287.\n\nWhen the cached  becomes invalid (e.g. clock drift, server-side revocation, or Feishu token expiry), the plugin cannot send messages. Error code  is returned, but the plugin does not automatically refresh the token and retry. Users must manually restart the gateway to recover.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n- : Added  /  for multi-callback cache invalidation.  detects 99991663/99991664.  retries once on token-invalid (separate  flag, independent of rate-limit budget). Fulfilled token-invalid bodies handled.\n- :  creates a plugin-owned  via .  expires  in the private cache by appId namespace.\n- : getter pattern —  inside request closure, ensures fresh client after cache clear.\n- :  registered. CardKit create retry on 99991663/99991664.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Live runtime proof (2026-07-02T09:02:48+00:00, host: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C, commit: ebaaf9d2a9)\n\n\n\n### Recovery path (production code)\n\n\n### Full test suite (90/90 passed)\n\n\n## AI Assistance\n\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
